# Kata class X runtime — NOT IMPLEMENTED IN-TREE.
#
# The architecture recognises Kata Containers as a second microVM backend for
# class X. This repository ships NO Kata VMRuntime. If AHP_COMPUTE_RUNTIME=kata
# the supervisor fails closed with:
#   "no in-tree Kata VMRuntime; supply one to NewSupervisor"
# It does NOT simulate a Kata VM.
#
# To enable Kata, an operator (or a future contractor) must:
#   1. implement a compute.VMRuntime backed by the Kata Containers API, and
#   2. pass it to compute.NewSupervisor(socket, rt) (e.g. via a build tag or a
#      supervisor variant cmd), and
#   3. provide the Kata-specific environment here.
#
# Until then this file documents the gate; nothing here is consumed at runtime.
AHP_COMPUTE_RUNTIME=kata
AHP_COMPUTE_SUPERVISOR_SOCKET=/run/ahp/compute-kata.sock
